            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0132" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg16"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811f.812/589b.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">To the Diplomatic Officers of the United
                    States</hi>.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: You are instructed to communicate to
                    the Governments to which you are respectively accredited the following
                    information relative to the opening of the Panama Canal, which has been
                    furnished by the Secretary of War: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Panama Canal will be opened for commerce to vessels not needing more
                            than 30 feet of water, on and after August 15, 1914.</p>
                        <p>The official opening of the canal, as heretofore announced, will be in
                            the month of March, 1915. An appropriate announcement will be made when
                            a greater depth of water than 30 feet has been secured.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
